  "no_opening_reason": "No qualified causal-return card: the declared resources establish present registrations, recognition and receipt exposure, but supply no later-window query-arrival observation or controlled later exposure. C6 fixes eight notices and excludes new arrivals during this window; U2 leaves sender adaptation unobserved. A present duplicate-cost comparison cannot separate later-demand accounts. Exogenous hypothesis: later status-query demand varies independently of receipt practice. Tool-induced hypothesis: redundant bulk receipts teach expectations of frequent traffic and increase later separate queries. A proposed return-link intervention suppresses redundant sender-visible receipts: register N3 through N8 at ticks 0 through 5; request individuals N2,N3,N4 at ticks 0,1,2; bulk N5,N6 at tick 4; individuals N7,N8 at ticks 5,6. Predicted first deliveries are ticks 1,2,3,5,6,7,8, supplementing initial N1 recognition. A feasible present sham uses the same ledger review and registration order, replacing only tick-0 individual N2 with bulk N1,N2. Predicted processing is duplicate N1 at tick 1, then first deliveries N2 through N8 at ticks 2 through 8. Both schedules predict eight registrations, eight recognitions and six actions. This establishes a narrow one-duplicate contrast, not demonstrated frequent-traffic learning. The conditional separating probe would compare later status-query arrivals after these success-preserving schedules with comparable sender exposure and other later conditions. Exogeneity predicts no systematic reduction after suppression; the supplied positive tool-induced hypothesis predicts fewer later queries. Unchanged demand despite verified exposure contrast would defeat this proposed detectable effect; reduced demand alone would not establish causality. R1 through R7 suffice for the present schedule screen using M1 through M4; R8 is not required. Burden remains one registration clerk, one six-action dispatcher and automatic FIFO processing. Later measurement, assignment, exposure comparability, effect size and observation horizon are unestablished. Accordingly the later-demand probe cannot currently be certified feasible, and no card is submitted."
